<p>This policy explains which data Devacancy collects, what we use it for, who we share it with, and how you control it. It follows Brazil's General Data Protection Law (LGPD) and is written to also meet the expectations of users in other countries. Questions? Write to <a href="mailto:suporte@devacancy.online">suporte@devacancy.online</a>.</p>

<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
<p>Devacancy is a platform that helps developers find jobs that match their profile and, with a subscription, sends applications on their behalf. Devacancy is the controller of the data described here. For any privacy matter, contact <a href="mailto:suporte@devacancy.online">suporte@devacancy.online</a>.</p>

<h2>2. Data we collect</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>What you give us:</strong> name, email, password (stored only in encrypted form, never as plain text), WhatsApp number, city, questionnaire answers and professional profile data (role, level, technologies, experience, education, languages, expected pay, LinkedIn, GitHub and portfolio links), summary, and your resume PDF. For companies: company name, contact role, website and hiring information.</li>
  <li><strong>From social login (Google, GitHub or LinkedIn):</strong> name, verified email, photo and the account identifier. We never receive your password from those services.</li>
  <li><strong>Payment data:</strong> payments are processed by Asaas (PIX and card), Stripe (card) or PayPal. We <strong>do not store card details</strong>; we only keep the plan, amount, status and transaction identifiers. With manual PIX you pay our account directly and we check the receipt.</li>
  <li><strong>Automatic data:</strong> IP address (to estimate your country, set currency and payment methods, and for security and fraud prevention), language, browser and access logs.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. What we use your data for</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Providing the service (performance of the contract):</strong> building your profile, finding matching jobs, sending applications on your behalf, unlocking your plan and support.</li>
  <li><strong>Payments and legal obligations:</strong> confirming payments, issuing receipts and meeting tax duties.</li>
  <li><strong>Security and improvement (legitimate interest):</strong> protecting accounts, preventing fraud and abuse, and understanding what to improve.</li>
  <li><strong>Communication:</strong> service emails such as password recovery and payment notices.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell your data and we do not make automated decisions that have legal effects on you.</p>

<h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Companies and recruiters:</strong> when we send an application on your behalf, the hiring company receives your profile data and resume. This is the purpose of the service you hired.</li>
  <li><strong>Payment processors:</strong> Asaas, Stripe and PayPal, to charge and confirm payments.</li>
  <li><strong>Infrastructure:</strong> hosting, email delivery and an approximate IP geolocation service (ipwho.is). Text fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, which sees your IP when delivering them.</li>
  <li><strong>Measurement and advertising (only with your consent):</strong> Google Analytics (Google) and the Meta Pixel (Facebook and Instagram), to measure how the site is used and whether our ads lead to sign-ups and subscriptions. See section 5.</li>
  <li><strong>Authorities:</strong> when required by law or court order.</li>
</ul>
<p>Some of these providers are located outside Brazil. In those cases, the international transfer happens to deliver the service you requested and with providers that apply protection measures compatible with the LGPD.</p>

<h2>5. Cookies</h2>
<p><strong>Essential (always on):</strong> the session cookie (keeps you signed in and protects forms), the language cookie and the one that stores your cookie choice. The site does not work properly without them.</p>
<p><strong>Measurement and advertising (only if you accept):</strong> when you click "Accept" on the cookie notice, we load Google Analytics and the Meta Pixel. They use cookies and identifiers to record the pages you visit, your device and browser, approximate location and key actions, such as creating an account or subscribing to a plan (with the amount and currency). We do not send your name, email, resume or password to these tools. Google and Meta process this data under their own policies and may use it to measure and optimize ads.</p>
<p>If you decline, these tools are not loaded. You can change your mind at any time using the "Cookies" link in the site footer, and you can also clear cookies in your browser.</p>

<h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
<p>For as long as your account exists. If you delete your account, we erase your profile, resume and personal data within 30 days, except what the law requires us to keep, such as payment and tax records (generally 5 years). Backups are discarded in the normal rotation cycle.</p>

<h2>7. Your rights</h2>
<p>You may ask for: confirmation that we process your data; access; correction; anonymization, blocking or deletion of unnecessary data; portability; information about who we share it with; and to withdraw consent. You can fix almost everything yourself under <strong>My profile</strong> and <strong>delete your account</strong> there at any time. For other requests, write to <a href="mailto:suporte@devacancy.online">suporte@devacancy.online</a>; we reply within 15 days.</p>

<h2>8. Security</h2>
<p>We use encrypted connections (HTTPS), password encryption, attempt limits against unauthorized access and restricted access to data. No system is 100% secure; if a relevant incident occurs, we will notify you and the Brazilian data protection authority as the law requires.</p>

<h2>9. Minors</h2>
<p>Devacancy is intended for people aged 18 or older.</p>

<h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>We may update this text. The date of the latest revision appears at the top of the page and, for important changes, we notify you by email or inside the site.</p>
